# Every service image builds from the repository root, so this list is the whole of what a builder is
# handed. It excludes only what a build never reads: the host's output trees, its secrets, and prose.
# Nothing here is an input one of the Dockerfiles names, and none of the workspace packages are removed
# (`turbo prune` decides which of those an image actually carries).

# Host build output. Every image compiles what it needs from source, and a host's tree is the wrong
# platform besides: `pnpm install` writes platform-specific binaries and `cargo` writes an ABI.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
target
**/target
.turbo
**/.turbo
# The host package store. Gitignored, so it was never a tracked input, but 700MB of it was still
# being shipped to the daemon on every build; the images mount their own store as a cache instead.
.pnpm-store
# tsc's incremental state, which records the host's paths and mtimes and can make a build skip emit.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# One build tree per creator's build. The runtime stage creates this empty and owned by `node`.
apps/grove/game-builder/.builds
# Prisma's generated client, regenerated by the api build.
**/src/generated

# Not a checkout. This is also why the root `prepare` has to tolerate a missing `.git` rather than
# assuming it can install hooks.
.git
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.vscode

# Secrets and local state. `.env.example` carries no secret and is documentation, so it stays out too.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
**/*.tfvars

# Prose, and the test files beside each package's sources. A `build` script compiles `src`.
*.md
**/*.md
docs
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx

# Terraform's, and a benchmark's readings.
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
bench/runs
*.log
